The school opened in 1870 and was located approximately 7 miles west of Geelong. It was a limestone building with an attached residence, erected by local residents. &nbsp;Head Teacher Lewis Walters taught at the school for 21 years.&nbsp;<br />
<br />
In February 1923, a new weatherboard school and residence was opened by Minister of Education, Sir Alexander Peacock.&nbsp;

This council was constituted in 1994 as part of a statewide program of local government reform enacted between 1993 and 1995. The reform process reduced the number of councils from 210 to 78. This council was appointed as a successor in law for the City of Brunswick (VA 2285), the City of Coburg (VA 2406) and part of the City of Broadmeadows (VA 2395). Any rights, assets and liabilities of the abolished council/s was assumed by The City of Moreland as its/their successor in law.<br />
<br />
On 13 September 2022, the name of this council was officially changed from Moreland City Council to Merri-bek City Council. The name legally took effect on 26 September 2022 (Victoria Government Gazette G37, 15 September 2022, pp. 3871).&nbsp;
